From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nura rc4 displayport series <rc4-displayport@nura.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: guacamole: add the DisplayPort audio link,
 disabled

Add the DPCM back end that would carry audio to the external display: CPU DAI
104 (DISPLAY_PORT_RX, AFE port 0x6020), platform q6routing, codec the DP
controller (which publishes an hdmi-codec DAI).  A link with both a platform
and a codec child is marked no_pcm by qcom_snd_parse_of(), so the machine
driver's prepare/hw_params/startup/shutdown hooks are installed for it.

The link is shipped with status = "disabled" and must stay that way for rc4.
Reason: ASoC binds every available DAI link when the card registers, and
snd_soc_add_pcm_runtime() returns -EPROBE_DEFER if any link's codec DAI is not
registered (sound/soc/soc-core.c).  The codec here is the DP controller's
hdmi-codec, which only exists once mdss_dp has probed.  qcom_snd_parse_of()
walks for_each_available_child_of_node(), so a disabled link is not part of the
card at all - but an enabled one couples the entire "OnePlus 7 Pro" card to the
DP controller: if DP failed to probe, there would be no speakers, no mic and no
headset either.  DP audio is unsolved on this SoC family anyway, so the default
must be video only.

Enabling it is a deliberate one-line experiment: status = "okay", rebuild, and
follow the DP audio ladder in the topic README (with the patches/0046-0050
series applied).  Nothing here is known to produce sound; the DSP is expected
to time out on port 0x6020.

Signed-off-by: Nura rc4 displayport series <rc4-displayport@nura.invalid>
---
 .../dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-displayport.dtsi         | 39 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-displayport.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-displayport.dtsi
index 5f2709d..6ecd0ce 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-displayport.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-displayport.dtsi
@@ -81,3 +81,42 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * DisplayPort audio: present but disabled by default.
+ *
+ * This is a DPCM back end (cpu + platform + codec), which is what makes the
+ * machine driver's prepare/hw_params/startup/shutdown hooks run for it.
+ *
+ * It stays at status = "disabled" on purpose.  ASoC binds every available DAI
+ * link when the sound card registers, and snd_soc_add_pcm_runtime() returns
+ * -EPROBE_DEFER when a link's codec DAI is not registered (sound/soc/
+ * soc-core.c).  qcom_snd_parse_of() only walks available children, so a
+ * disabled link is not part of the card at all; if it were enabled and the DP
+ * controller (the hdmi-codec's parent device) failed to probe, the whole
+ * "OnePlus 7 Pro" card would never register: no speakers, no mic, no
+ * headset.  DP audio is also unsolved on this SoC family, so the safe default
+ * is video only.
+ *
+ * To run the experiment, change this to status = "okay", rebuild, and follow
+ * the DP audio ladder in the topic README.  Expect the DSP to time out on
+ * port 0x6020; nothing here is known to produce sound.
+ */
+&sound {
+	dp-dai-link {
+		status = "disabled";
+		link-name = "DisplayPort Playback";
+
+		cpu {
+			sound-dai = <&q6afedai DISPLAY_PORT_RX>;
+		};
+
+		platform {
+			sound-dai = <&q6routing>;
+		};
+
+		codec {
+			sound-dai = <&mdss_dp>;
+		};
+	};
+};
-- 
